  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Given that $C$ and $D$ are finite, non-overlapping regions and that\n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A=12,\\,{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A=-8,\n$$\n\nfind the value of \n\n$$\n{\u222c}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A.\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "Using the linearity and additivity of double integrals, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\u222c}_{C\\cup D}3f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A & =3{\u222c}_{C\\cup D}f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A \\\\  & =3({\u222c}_{C}f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A+{\u222c}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{\u00a0}\\text{d}A) \\\\  & =3(12-8) \\\\  & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$",
